Delta since v13 touching WS-D: (1) the peel's admission: B = 1.96e7 is now a WORK bound chosen for coverage (admitted corner n=2000 d<=980, n=1001 d<=2175; the edge W=B at d=980), no longer derived from an observed rate; the peel's time is an ESTIMATE from a mechanical extraction over every GUARDIANN-PEEL-CORNER-TIMING line of every bound run (rfcs/257-java-upgrade-audit/ws-d-oracle/corner-refit-rates.py and .txt: 116 timings over 7 logs, 98 nonzero rates, min 4.13e-8 median 7.22e-8 max 1.75e-7 s per n*d), the 1007 consequence owned; oracle README item 31 added, item 29's claims superseded; (2) phase D-0 rewritten (section 5 'Decision (v14)' and Fixtures): the route owns every commit of its owners (the DDL body and catalog bootstrap committed in-body so hooks ran twice; those in-body commits go and a self-committing body fails structurally with BodyCommittedError); owners that retry outside the route (the queue drain's throttled iterator, AutoContinuingCursor with its 1031 arm declared, the heartbeat cleanup) are a named census class with the target's bound and predicate each; 1079/1235/1242 dropped from the route's list; the client's 1200 leaves the record layer as a CLIENT prerequisite (libfdb_c waits for commit proxies inside its commit and returns 1021; the pure-Go client is to do the same, under the client review gate); SPFresh's split-window signal (SPFreshSplitWindowError) consumes no attempt, keeping RFC-094's foreground contract (v13's 'far inside ten attempts' withdrawn); chaos arms fire at most once per attempt-loop call, plus an explicit FaultEveryAttempt arm for exhaustion; the route is a call argument, not a context value; the delay waits on the DST SimClock; EXHAUSTED is reconciled as an unknown outcome by the hunts and the chaos model; the census is counted on the reviewed tree; (3) PRODUCTION CHANGE landed ahead of D-0: SimFDB's retry limit returns the BODY's error chain (declinedRetryError) instead of a bare code (pkg/simfdb/simfdb.go; pinned by TestSimRetryLimit_DeclinedRetryKeepsTheBodysErrorChain in pkg/simfdb/retry_limit_test.go; a mutation reddens it); (4) RFC-094 section 2 foreground paragraph and its :202/:477 references updated; TODO.md transactor claims scoped; the pkg/relational/core/embedded/connection.go:46 comment corrected. NOT WS-D, same tree, own gates: WS-F v3 (ws-f-design.md, conformance/ws_f_probe_conformance_test.go, conformance/wsf_record_layer_probe.java, sql_plan_steps.java, plandiff go_runner.go and the renamed docscheck allowlist entry go_runner.go:withEphemeralSchema in pkg/docscheck/dst_seam_gate_test.go), WS-C design text r9 (NAK, being revised), WS-J v13 and WS-E v11 (NAKs; their review directories are excluded from this tree).
